      "start": 38.05779166666667,
      "end": 54.918375,
      "lesson_progress": 0.375,
      "text": "Put the parts together. Four point seven two six equals four, plus zero point seven, plus zero point zero two, plus zero point zero zero six. The digits describe different sized parts, so their positions matter just as much as they do in whole numbers.",
      "chapter": "Expand the decimal",
